From f812dfe28464b784c43b79df2f996469f4f3b491 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Walters <jackwalterswork@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:24:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] git_ui: Draw merge request threads like the threads on
 lines

A thread on the merge request itself had its own look, with Reply and
Resolve as text buttons, and its own Start Thread button in the title
row. It is now drawn with the parts of a thread on a line: the same
chip when folded, and when open the same comment card with the draft,
reply and resolve icon buttons, the same indented replies, and a
one-line reply box where Enter sends. A reply can be drafted with the
model here too, from the thread alone, since it has no code of its own.

The Start Thread button is gone from the title row. The comments menu
has the entry that opens the box for a new thread, lists these threads
with the comments on lines, counts them, and is shown for any merge
request, even one with no comment yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
